  "resolution_html": "<p>Outlook.com (web version) doesn't have a direct export option, but you can still save your emails by connecting your webmail to an email client like Outlook or Thunderbird. Here's how to do it: </p>\n<p><strong><em>Method 1: Export via Outlook Desktop</em> </strong></p>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Set Up Outlook Desktop App</strong>: </li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Download and install the <strong>Outlook desktop app</strong> if you don’t have it</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Add your <strong>Outlook.com</strong> email account (go to <strong>File</strong> &gt; <strong>Add Account</strong>)</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>Sync Your Emails</strong>: </li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Wait for all your emails to sync into the desktop app</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Export Your Emails to PST</strong>: </li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>Follow the steps above (see Method 1 under Outlook Desktop App)</li>\n</ul>",
